 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Provides, in tort cases where one defendant has settled, that remaining defendants must elect, prior to trial, whether to reduce liability by the amount of the settlement or by the amount of the equitable share of damages delegated to the settler in the verdict.",
 "title": "Provides, in tort cases where one defendant has settled, that remaining defendants must elect prior to trial as to reduction in liability; repealer",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "S6081",
     "basePrintNoStr": "S6081-2019",
     "printNo": "S6081",
     "session": 2019,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 282\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6081, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the general obligations law, in relation to settle-\n      ments  in  tort  actions; and to repeal section 15-108 of such law\n      relating to release or covenant not to sue\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require non-settling defendants  in  tort  actions  to\nelect  their judgment reduction before the commencement of trial. In the\nabsence of available settlement information, the  potential  exists  for\nnon-settling  defendants  to pay more than their equitable share and for\nplaintiffs to become unjustly enriched by receiving monetary amounts  in\nexcess of the rendered verdict.\n\n  I  support the public policy of this bill which encourages settlements\nin civil actions, however, the proposed legislation is not an  effective\nmeans  to that end. Numerous stakeholders have raised concerns with this\napproach, with many stating this change will unfairly  tip  the  balance\ntoo  far  in favor of a settlement. Based on the foregoing reasons, I am\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 282,
